 <693558+janosmiko@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Tue, 11 Aug 2026 10:57:53 +0200
Subject: [PATCH 062/154] chore: say what the command route and the save-page
 path actually did
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

Two blind spots a VM scenario cannot see past. The command route logged nothing
about whether the core claimed a command, so "claimed and dropped here" and
"fell through to the stock handler, which then did nothing" looked identical.
SavePage opens a sheet, so nothing observable said the command arrived at all;
the line is anchored to the tab id so a probe can tell which window's tab ran
it.

Signed-off-by: János Mikó <693558+janosmiko@users.noreply.github.com>
---
 chrome/browser/ui/browser_commands.cc | 6 ++++++
 1 file changed, 6 insertions(+)

diff --git a/chrome/browser/ui/browser_commands.cc b/chrome/browser/ui/browser_commands.cc
index 83efe1922093d..1e5bff9fbf6fd 100644
--- a/chrome/browser/ui/browser_commands.cc
+++ b/chrome/browser/ui/browser_commands.cc
@@ -16,6 +16,7 @@
 #include "base/command_line.h"
 #include "base/feature_list.h"
 #include "base/i18n/rtl.h"
+#include "base/logging.h"
 #include "base/memory/scoped_refptr.h"
 #include "base/metrics/field_trial_params.h"
 #include "base/metrics/histogram_functions.h"
@@ -64,6 +65,7 @@
 #include "chrome/browser/ui/autofill/payments/offer_notification_bubble_controller_impl.h"
 #include "chrome/browser/ui/autofill/payments/save_card_bubble_controller_impl.h"
 #include "chrome/browser/ui/autofill/payments/virtual_card_enroll_bubble_controller_impl.h"
+#include "chrome/browser/ui/atrium/atrium_browser_controller.h"
 #include "chrome/browser/ui/bookmarks/bookmark_bar_controller.h"
 #include "chrome/browser/ui/bookmarks/bookmark_stats.h"
 #include "chrome/browser/ui/bookmarks/bookmark_utils.h"
@@ -2208,6 +2210,10 @@ void SavePage(BrowserWindowInterface* browser) {
   WebContents* current_tab =
       browser->GetTabStripModel()->GetActiveWebContents();
   DCHECK(current_tab);
+  // The save panel is a sheet, so nothing observable says the
+  // command reached here. Anchored to the tab id so a probe can tell which
+  // window's tab it ran on.
+  VLOG(1) << "Atrium: tab " << atrium::TabId(current_tab) << " save page";
   if (current_tab->GetContentsMimeType() == "application/pdf") {
     base::RecordAction(UserMetricsAction("PDF.SavePage"));
 #if BUILDFLAG(ENABLE_PDF)
